WEBVTT

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.170
"CELL"

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:54.460
"EPISODE 4:
H. PYLORI"

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.380
"EPISODE 4:
H. PYLORI"
"H. Pylori."

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.170
"EPISODE 4:
H. PYLORI"

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:00.040
"FRAGILE"
"CONDENSED GAS"

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:03.290
There are virus-infected cells here, too!

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:15.170
We have a situation near the pharynx.

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:18.170
Immune Cells...
are to head to the site immediately!

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:19.880
"WHITE BLOOD CELL"
Target sighted!

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:22.080
Come on, come on, come on!

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.080
We're going to slaughter 'em all!

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.420
Die!

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:27.620
Don't let any get away!

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.540
Die!

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:36.750
And so, it's the same old, same old again today.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.120
The Immune Cells come swooping in,

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:44.790
defeat the infected bad guys,
and now the town is peaceful again.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:47.500
And so, just like any other day,

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:52.040
we ordinary cells are stuck
on the sidelines again.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:57.080
What a drag!

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:01.750
I mean, those Immune guys just don't play fair!

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:04.750
"OUT OF ORDER"
The way they put on that whole superhero act
when they're just a bunch of assassins...

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.620
The way they put on that whole superhero act
when they're just a bunch of assassins...

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.830
And then, when we get attacked
by viruses, they're like...

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:11.880
..."It's your own fault for not
protecting yourselves!"

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:15.620
or "You should've done your homework!"

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.210
Jeez.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:21.830
Just once in my life, if someone would say,
"Thank you for rescuing me!"

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:25.170
What wouldn't I give to hear those words?

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:32.880
If only I was stronger!

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.420
Nyuuu!

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:38.750
Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.830
G-G-Germs?

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:44.960
Oh man, I've stumbled upon something I shouldn't
have! I've got to let the Immune Cells know!

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:48.830
Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.670
Wh-What's wrong?

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:53.580
--Nyuuu!
--You can't get out of there?

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:57.830
You're germs! Don't beg a cell for help!

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:01.080
Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:03.040
What am I going to do?

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:06.540
I'll help you, but you'd better go back
to where you came from, okay?

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:09.170
What, are you still babies?

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:11.000
That's it! You've got this!

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.710
You can do it! Almost there!

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:16.920
Nyuuu!

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:21.040
Look at those happy faces.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:23.250
Hey, I just rescued some germs.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:24.040
Oh man.

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:25.670
Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:30.420
Hey, don't get attached to me!
You guys are germs, aren't you?

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:33.580
Hey! Ordinary Cell there!
What are you being so sneaky about?

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.000
N-N-N-N-Nothing! It's nothing!

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:41.960
I just kind of overate! I wasn't feeling well,
so I decided to crouch here to rest!

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.790
Is that right? Take care, then!

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:51.040
Jeez, that was close! There's no telling
what they would do if they spotted you.

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:52.420
Nyuuu!

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:54.790
Now, be good and go back
to where you came from.

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:56.830
--Nyuuu?
--See ya.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.500
Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:03.330
Hey, stop following me, dammit!

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:05.710
I don't want to get yelled at, all right?

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:08.500
--I'll pretend I never saw you,
so try to make it back to--

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:10.670
--Nyuuu?
--I'll pretend I never saw you,
so try to make it back to--

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:19.080
Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:21.290
"NYUUU'
Nyuuu!

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:25.420
I went and brought them home.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:29.080
Jeez, this is bad!
I'm so going to get yelled at!

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:32.790
Wait, worst case, I could get killed, too!

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:44.120
My receptor's definitely picking something up,

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:46.000
so where are the antigens?

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.170
Hey, White Blood Cell!

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:50.620
Thank you for saving us earlier!

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.000
Sure.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.000
Is something the matter?

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:58.120
No. I've been patrolling this
area for antigens, and...

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:00.750
Not at home?

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:04.670
Hello? I've come to deliver your oxygen!

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:05.790
Ordinary Cell?

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:06.540
Nyuuu!

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:07.920
"NYUUU"
Nyuuu!

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:10.540
Dummies! Shush! Shush!

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:13.960
Keep it down, all right?
If we're caught, they're going to kill you!

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:17.790
Hello? Cell boy? Are you in there?

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:20.750
No answer, huh?

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:23.460
Do you think maybe he
was talking in his sleep?

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:24.670
Well, never mind.

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:28.000
I have to find those antigens first.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:29.170
No, hold up!

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:33.420
Maybe the antigen's threatening
Cell boy inside there,

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:35.120
and there's no way for him to call for help,

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:39.080
so he emitted that sound
just now as a last resort?

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.170
If you call for help, you're dead!

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:43.290
"NYUUU"
Nyuuu!

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:46.170
I-It's all quiet out there now.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:47.750
Are they gone?

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:49.120
All right.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:51.620
I'm going to slip out now
and take them back.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:56.210
Hey, Cell boy! Are you okay?
I'm coming to save you now!

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:04.120
Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:05.670
And what exactly...

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:07.290
...is your explanation for this?

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:11.920
--Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!
--W-Well, long story short, I rescued them,
but then they got attached to me.

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:16.170
And when I thought about them being killed,
I couldn't turn my back on them.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:18.330
I see.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:21.620
I can see how it'd be hard
to turn your back on them.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:26.330
--Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!
--Oh? You're hungry?

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:28.040
I don't have anything for you.

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:30.750
I said, I have nothing. See?

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:33.080
Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:34.500
Cell boy...

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:36.420
I understand how you feel,

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:40.580
but I can't allow germs
to multiply inside this body.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:45.750
Once they multiply, germs go on to release
toxins, harming the cells inside the body.

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:49.290
In some cases, this could trigger hemolysis
which would destroy the Red Blood Cells

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:52.620
or take away their nutrients.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:54.120
You understand, right?

00:07:56.710 --> 00:08:00.000
I guess it would be cruel
to do it before his eyes.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.750
Thank you for your help
in capturing the antigens.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:03.290
Oh...

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:09.960
Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:12.120
This is No. 4989!

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:14.580
We're battling germs in the stomach,
and it's not looking good!

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:17.380
We need your backup right away!

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:19.580
Roger that! I'm on my way!

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:23.620
Cell boy, sorry, but I'm taking
custody of these germs!

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:27.460
Ordinary Cell?

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:29.620
S-Sure, of course.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:31.830
He's only doing his job.

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:35.880
Protecting us all is the
Immune Cells' job, after all.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:40.380
U-Uh...

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:42.920
Hey, wait, Ordinary Cell!

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:45.080
Sign this!

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:53.580
That's right! Run around in a frenzy!

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:55.620
What's going on?

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:57.000
Where's the enemy?

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:59.380
Hey, 1146!

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:01.960
Um, it's on the other side of that wall!

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:07.790
Pylori!

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:08.960
H. pylori.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:10.500
Resistant to gastric acid.

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:15.920
Can trigger gastrointestinal diseases, causing
ulcers and sometimes leading to stomach cancer.

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:19.960
It's a type of harmful bacteria,
detrimental to the human body.

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:22.960
Officially known as "Helicobacter pylori."

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:27.000
H. pylori? Who would've thought?

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:31.000
There's nothing you cells can do to stop me!

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:36.210
We H. pylori have bodies that are tough
as nails, so we can operate in gastric acid!

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:40.420
Unlike you lot!

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:42.750
It's like chaos here!

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:45.250
So, this is the front line, huh?

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:48.620
Nyuuu...

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:54.290
B-But it's not like we can go to him, you know!
We'll get dissolved in that gastric acid!

00:09:54.290 --> 00:09:55.540
I'll go!

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:57.830
I'll land a fatal blow on him
before I get dissolved!

00:09:57.830 --> 00:10:02.210
What? But 1146, if you do that, you'll die!

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:05.170
There's no way around it!
It's for the sake of this body!

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:06.750
For the sake of this body...

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:09.880
That's right. It's for the sake of this body.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:14.080
To die for someone else's sake...
How cool is that?

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:16.250
For someone like me...

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:20.580
For a humble ordinary cell like me,
that would be impossible.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:22.920
How powerless am I anyway?

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:26.830
This world belongs to the H. pylori now!

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:29.380
Oh, crap! The stomach lining!

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:33.620
At least put this on!
It's made of acid-resistant enamel!

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:35.750
It's crumbling!

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:38.380
Look out!

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:47.750
C-Cell boy!

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:54.830
Sorry. I'm nothing but an ordinary cell,

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:59.790
so I can't protect you like I should.

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:04.380
You guys are bacteria inside this body,
so you're going to end up dead.

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:05.790
But you know what?

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:09.620
I would've saved you if I could.

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:14.960
Just remember that you did have
somebody who cared about you.

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:20.580
Well, now, I've seen everything!
A cell, protecting germs?

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:24.920
Hmm... I just know I've seen
you somewhere before.

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:26.080
Are you all right?

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:30.080
Oh, never mind! I'm going to
eliminate you all in one go!

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:33.540
Take this! Gastric Acid Hell!

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:34.920
Uh-oh!

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:37.580
Nyuuu!

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:42.420
Those germs opened up a hole,
so now we have a pathway!

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:45.290
This is our chance to take over this--

00:11:45.290 --> 00:11:46.210
Nyuuu?

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:47.920
Nyuuu!

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:48.920
Huh?

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:51.620
The other germs that happened to
show up just got turned into slush!

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:53.620
Can you believe how powerful that was?

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:57.040
Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:01.380
W-Wait! One's missing!

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:07.620
No way! So, I guess he's--

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:13.040
Nyuuu...

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:15.670
Hey, he's alive!

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:19.880
Wh-What's going on?

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:22.080
That germ's acting...

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:36.880
Wh-What was that? Did the H. pylori
just take a hit from that germ's attack?

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:43.380
Grrr! I-Impossible! You actually
dared to inflict a wound on me?

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:46.170
Huh? W-Wait, don't tell me you're...

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:47.920
...a lactic acid bacterium?

00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:51.120
Nyuuu!

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:52.710
Lactic acid bacteria.

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:55.960
Rather than refer to a specific bacteria,
it is the blanket term for germs

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:58.750
that produce lactic acid in massive quantities

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:03.750
by breaking down sugars to produce
the energy necessary for growth.

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:05.540
Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:09.000
Stop it!

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:13.380
I can't take this!
My only option is to flee-- Oh no...

00:13:13.380 --> 00:13:16.120
You finally came out from the sea of acid!

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:18.120
N-N-N-Now I've done it!

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:20.170
Nyuuu!

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:22.040
You pylo-ing scum...

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:23.040
Die!

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:24.250
Nyuuu!

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:27.540
Pylori!

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:31.920
Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:36.290
D-Did he just beat that huge H. pylori?

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:38.120
Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:39.920
Wh-Wh-What's up with you guys?

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:43.380
Hey, don't jump on me! You're all covered
in gastric acid! It's bad for me!

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:46.120
Hey, are those germs...

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:50.080
--Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!
--Yeah. It looks like it.

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:51.920
Cell boy...

00:13:51.920 --> 00:13:53.080
I'm so sorry!

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:55.540
After what just happened, I get it now...

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:58.040
...exactly what kind of germs those guys are.

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:00.670
Nyuuu!

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:02.670
Those germs...

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:06.880
...are good bacteria that work
for the sake of this body.

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:08.750
Good bacteria.

00:14:08.750 --> 00:14:11.500
The layperson's term for the bacteria
found in the digestive system

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:16.210
that are beneficial
for the human body's health.

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:19.500
Well-known examples include
lactic acid and lactobacillus bifidus.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:22.880
Some lactic acid bacteria
are resistant to gastric acid

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:27.380
and can suppress the activation of H. pylori.

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:30.580
Nyuuu!

00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:35.750
They must've entered this body
along with food or something.

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:40.330
I've never seen them in an inactive state,
so I didn't realize it at first.

00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:44.080
All right, I have to get back to patrol duty.

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:48.330
Because bacteria might invade
through that hole the H. pylori ripped open.

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:51.250
B-But what about these guys?

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:01.290
Hey, you want to go to your friends, don't you?

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:02.750
Nyuuu!

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:05.960
Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:09.120
I can't go with you. I'll melt.

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:10.380
Nyuuu?

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:12.750
Nyuuu... Nyuuu...

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:14.080
Nyuuu?

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:17.750
Go on.

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:20.210
Nyuuu...

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:23.000
Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.920
Take care of yourself.

00:15:26.750 --> 00:15:29.290
All right, Cell boy...

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:33.080
I'm about to tell you something
that has nothing to do with you.

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:35.620
There are all kinds of types
of lactic acid bacteria,

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:40.880
and I hear they all work with their friends
near different digestive organs.

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:44.670
I'm heading out to patrol those areas now.

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:46.580
Wanna come along?

00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:47.960
Yeah!

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:51.880
Hey!

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:54.500
So, there you are, Ordinary Cell!

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:56.460
I was wondering where you'd gone!

00:15:56.460 --> 00:15:58.500
If you could just stamp that receipt...

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:01.750
...or your signature will do, too.
Right here, please.

00:16:01.750 --> 00:16:03.880
Sorry, I forgot all about that.

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:06.120
Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:10.670
Ordinary Cell, haven't you put on
some weight since I last saw you?

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:14.080
Huh? Oh, yeah...

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:21.250
"ANTIGENIC SHIFT"

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:23.330
"ANTIGENIC SHIFT"
"Antigenic Shift."

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:24.920
"ANTIGENIC SHIFT"

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:25.710
"SMALL INTESTINE"

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:29.210
All right, I'm heading this way.

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:31.170
Right.

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:33.120
Good work!

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:35.210
"WELCOME TO THE SMALL INTESTINE"

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:40.290
This is the small intestine.

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:46.040
Okay! Hoist up the microvilli
from No. 1 through 10!

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:48.670
