00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:09.540
So, this is what these lactic acid bacteria do?

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:14.620
Lactic acid bacteria coexist with cells in
the body in various ways according to type.

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:18.120
These guys can make friends
with all kinds of cells!

00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:20.120
That's incredible!

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:25.080
I guess the small intestine might be
the ideal place for those germs to live.

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:26.500
Yeah.

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:28.830
Hey!

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:29.920
Nyuuu?

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:32.120
Nyu-nyu-nyuuu!

00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:36.540
Take care.

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:45.880
Well, who knew? Lactic acid bacteria
really does a lot for the body, huh?

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:48.210
Do these guys totally rock or what?

00:19:48.210 --> 00:19:50.920
Well, don't get too carried away, Cell boy.

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:53.710
They may be useful, but germs are germs.

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:57.670
If they ever start acting sketchy,
I'm going to deal with them right away.

00:19:57.670 --> 00:20:01.330
And one more thing. Whatever you do,
don't ever let anyone see them.

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:03.710
If any of the other Immune Cells spot them, I--

00:20:03.710 --> 00:20:05.710
Hey, check this out, will you?

00:20:05.710 --> 00:20:07.170
--Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!
--Ta-da!

00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:10.420
A lactic acid bacterium in the hand
and one on the head!

00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:13.330
These guys are so fluffy and adorable!

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:15.880
Go ahead and pet them, White Blood Cell!

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:17.880
Huh? Germs nearby? My receptor!

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:19.670
Moron! Hide them!
Do you want them to get killed?

00:20:19.670 --> 00:20:21.500
Whoa! Don't yell at me!

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:23.880
Huh? There's nothing here.

00:20:23.880 --> 00:20:26.880
--Wh-Whoa!
--Malfunction, I guess. This receptor of mine...

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:30.250
Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:32.790
--Nyuuu!
--The lactic acid bacterium!

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:34.500
--Come back here!
--Cell boy!

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:37.330
Nyuuu!

00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:40.080
--Nyuuu!
--Lactic Acid Bacterium!

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:46.790
What should I do? It's too dangerous
for him to be on his own!

00:20:46.790 --> 00:20:47.880
I have to look for him!

00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:51.960
But there's no telling where
he'll end up inside this vast body.

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:56.080
I know! White Blood Cell, can you notify
the other Immune Cells right now?

00:20:56.080 --> 00:20:59.290
Tell them not to kill
that lactic acid bacterium!

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:01.750
I'm sorry. I can't do that.

00:21:01.750 --> 00:21:05.670
We Neutrophils are unable to present antigens.

00:21:05.670 --> 00:21:12.830
I can't tell other Immune Cells not to
attack him because he's good bacteria.

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:18.210
If he reaches an Immune Cell who can see
that he's good bacteria, he'll be fine.

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:21.080
But if he gets dealt with
as a mere foreign substance,

00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:23.290
then it would be out of my hands.

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:24.380
Sorry.

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:26.710
No way.

00:21:26.710 --> 00:21:28.830
Nyuuu?

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:33.580
I don't get it, White Blood Cell.

00:21:33.580 --> 00:21:36.000
You know he's not a bad guy.

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:38.580
Right. Even still...

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:44.210
That little guy... That little guy must've given
it all for this this body, too! I know it!

00:21:44.210 --> 00:21:47.420
Why would you kill someone like that?

00:21:47.420 --> 00:21:50.880
You Immune Cells are jerks!

00:21:50.880 --> 00:21:52.540
That's...

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:54.580
That's my...

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:55.790
That's our...

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:58.620
It's our job, that's why.

00:21:58.620 --> 00:22:00.750
That voice just now...

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:04.830
Long time no see.

00:22:04.830 --> 00:22:06.880
NK Cell!

